  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "lapsed_date": "01/09/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "While the external appearance would be similar to the existing dwellinghouse, the proposed resultant two-storey dwelling would unacceptably alter the nature of the existing bungalow by increasing its height and depth, appearing as an incongruous and tall addition to the existing house that would be visible from public vintage points along Oakwood due to its sitting on a higher ground than Nos. 60 and 62 Woodcote Avenue and its close proximity to adjacent rear gardens. The proposal would therefore not only fail to reflect the restricted and narrow character of the site and the low nature of the bungalow, but would also adversely impact on the open character and appearance of the immediate and surrounding area, comprising amenity spaces to east, west and north of the site, characterised with low, or no outbuildings within their rear gardens and so detracting from the appearance of the street scene within ASLC. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies 28 and 30 of the Sutton Local Plan and AA.2 (3)(a)(ii) of Class AA of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the General Permitted Development Order 2015 (as amended).\r",
    "Due to the depth, height, siting on a higher ground in relation to neighbouring properties to the east and north, the close proximity of the dwelling to neighbouring occupiers, and without evidence to the contrary in the form of a light report, the proposed development would adversely affect the amenity of No. 62 Woodcote Avenue in terms of a loss of light to their rear garden, and adversely affect the amenity of No. 60 and 62 Woodcote Avenue and odd-numbered properties fronting Dower Avenue by way of a loss of outlook. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan and AA.2 (3)(a)(i) of Class AA of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the General Permitted Development Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The proposal would introduce first floor level windows facing directly the rear amenity area of No. 62 Woodcote Avenue where first floor openings do not exist, as such, the proposal would adversely affect the amenity of the adjoining occupiers by way of a loss of privacy, contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan and AA.2 (3)(a)(i) of Class AA of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the General Permitted Development Order 2015 (as amended)."
  ],
